Local patch 0105 (qwen3.6-35b-a3b-exl3-tensorfold): prefill steps under concurrency, chunk setting, 6-bit prompt launch.

Why: with several requests, the 35B's concurrent decoder prefills a waiting prompt STEP = 1024 rows a round; the EXL3
prompt experts cost 5.2 us a row at 1024 rows vs 2.8 at 4096 (each pass re-reads every expert), so concurrent prefill
ran ~35% below a lone prompt's.
What:
- qwen3_5_moe/cuda/multi.py: STEP from TF_PREFILL_STEP (default 1024 = upstream; the recipe sets 4096). Measured
  (8 streams): prefill 2.5k -> 3.5k tok/s (2k prompts), 3.1k -> 4.0k (8.8k prompts); decode unchanged; replies equal.
- qwen3_5/cuda/prefill.py CHUNK from TF_PREFILL_CHUNK (default 4096 = upstream), qwen3_5_moe/cuda/exl3.py scratch rows
  follow it. 8192 gives ~+4% prefill for +1.3 GiB admission (less context): off by default.
- cuda/exl3/experts_prefill.cuh prefill_widths (needs 0102): 6-bit experts with a wider shared one (this model) get
  their own launch sized for 6 bits (K 64 a stage) instead of the 16-bit one (K 32): bit-identical, ~4% faster.

diff --git a/src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_prefill.cuh b/src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_prefill.cuh
index 1d57120..647a514 100644
--- a/src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_prefill.cuh
+++ b/src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts_prefill.cuh
@@ -354,6 +354,11 @@ void prefill_widths(const PrefillArgs& a, cudaStream_t stream) {
     constexpr int W = 1, M = 8, T = 2, B = 64, S = 2;  // N warps, 128 members, 16 * N * T columns, K 64 a stage, 2 deep
     if (a.lo <= 8 && a.hi >= 8) prefill_go<CB, 8, 8, W, N, M, T, B, S>(a, stream);
     if (a.lo == 8 && a.hi == 8) return;
+    if (a.lo == 12 && a.hi > 12) {                     // 6-bit experts with a wider shared one (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B):
+        prefill_go<CB, 12, 12, W, N, M, T, B, S>(a, stream);          // the 6-bit ones K 64 a stage, sized for them
+        prefill_go<CB, 2, 16, W, N, M, T, 32, 2>(a, stream, 12);      // the rest as before
+        return;
+    }
     if (a.hi <= 12) prefill_go<CB, 2, 12, W, N, M, T, B, S>(a, stream, 8);   // e.g. a 6-bit shared expert
     else prefill_go<CB, 2, 16, W, N, M, T, 32, 2>(a, stream, 8);           // up to 8 bits: K 32 a stage fits
 }
